#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Grant writing for quantum computing {#grant-writing-for-quantum-computing}"
msgstr ""
"Penulisan hibah untuk komputasi kuantum {#grant-writing-for-quantum-"
"computing}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a leader of a quantum initiative, you likely know how to write grants "
"very well. It would not be useful to repeat here what you already know. "
"Rather, here we will take a few example practices for general grant writing "
"and map them into the space of quantum computing. To be clear, IBM "
"Quantum&reg; cannot tell you how to win grants; each funding agency has its "
"own priorities and each research group has its own strengths. We can, "
"however, share with you what deliverables we think are plausible, useful, "
"and exciting, as well as our perspective on the field.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai pemimpin inisiatif kuantum, kamu mungkin sudah tahu cara menulis "
"hibah dengan sangat baik. Tidak akan berguna untuk mengulangi di sini apa "
"yang sudah kamu ketahui. Sebaliknya, di sini kita akan mengambil beberapa "
"contoh praktik penulisan hibah umum dan memetakannya ke dalam ruang "
"komputasi kuantum. Jelas, IBM Quantum&reg; tidak bisa memberi tahu kamu cara"
" memenangkan hibah; setiap lembaga pendanaan memiliki prioritasnya sendiri "
"dan setiap kelompok penelitian memiliki kekuatannya sendiri. Namun, kita "
"bisa berbagi dengan kamu apa yang menurut kami dapat diwujudkan, berguna, "
"dan menarik, serta perspektif kita tentang bidang ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this guide, we will examine the following well-known practices in grant "
"writing, from the perspective of quantum computing:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam panduan ini, kita akan memeriksa praktik-praktik penulisan hibah yang "
"terkenal berikut, dari perspektif komputasi kuantum:\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "General practices {#general-practices}"
msgstr "Praktik umum {#general-practices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Finding grants**\n"
"* Start with a thorough overview of grants available to increase chances and optimize fit.\n"
"* Match agency initiatives (both strategic goals and timelines).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mencari hibah**\n"
"* Mulai dengan tinjauan menyeluruh tentang hibah yang tersedia untuk meningkatkan peluang dan mengoptimalkan kesesuaian.\n"
"* Cocokkan inisiatif lembaga (tujuan strategis maupun timeline).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Prior to writing proposal** (these are called out in the proposal itself)\n"
"* Carry out initial work as proof of principle and highlight it in the proposal (preferably work that is successful but that cannot be grown without funding).\n"
"* Demonstrate initiative in building collaborations (intra-university, regionally through QICs, nationally).\n"
"* Apply for and win seed funding as a multiplier of later grant outcomes.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Sebelum menulis proposal** (hal-hal ini disebutkan dalam proposal itu sendiri)\n"
"* Lakukan pekerjaan awal sebagai bukti prinsip dan soroti dalam proposal (sebaiknya pekerjaan yang berhasil tetapi tidak bisa berkembang tanpa pendanaan).\n"
"* Tunjukkan inisiatif dalam membangun kolaborasi (intra-universitas, secara regional melalui QIC, secara nasional).\n"
"* Lamar dan menangkan pendanaan awal sebagai pengganda hasil hibah selanjutnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**In the proposal**\n"
"* Call out the preliminary work above.\n"
"* Propose realistic work in terms of timelines, in-house expertise, the state of the science, collaborations, and funds.\n"
"* Outline institutional resources, facilities, and partnerships that increase feasibility.\n"
"* Demonstrate that the problem you are pursuing is important and is not solved. This also highlights mastery of recent progress in the field.\n"
"* Describe the expertise and credentials of the research team.\n"
"* List concrete deliverables that are realistic given the resources requested and time constraints.\n"
"* Acknowledge risks and provide realistic mitigation strategies.\n"
"* Provide a clear, coherent approach with concrete methods, datasets, activities, milestones, and decision points.\n"
"* Address rigor and reproducibility including data quality, controls, analysis and sharing.\n"
"* Draw connections between academia and industry, and broader impacts generally.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Dalam proposal**\n"
"* Sebutkan pekerjaan awal di atas.\n"
"* Usulkan pekerjaan yang realistis dalam hal timeline, keahlian internal, keadaan ilmu pengetahuan, kolaborasi, dan dana.\n"
"* Uraikan sumber daya, fasilitas, dan kemitraan institusional yang meningkatkan kelayakan.\n"
"* Tunjukkan bahwa masalah yang kamu kejar penting dan belum terpecahkan. Ini juga menyoroti penguasaan kemajuan terkini di bidang ini.\n"
"* Jelaskan keahlian dan kredensial tim penelitian.\n"
"* Daftarkan deliverable konkret yang realistis mengingat sumber daya yang diminta dan batasan waktu.\n"
"* Akui risiko dan berikan strategi mitigasi yang realistis.\n"
"* Berikan pendekatan yang jelas dan koheren dengan metode, dataset, aktivitas, milestone, dan titik keputusan yang konkret.\n"
"* Tangani ketelitian dan reproduktibilitas termasuk kualitas data, kontrol, analisis, dan berbagi.\n"
"* Bangun koneksi antara akademisi dan industri, serta dampak yang lebih luas secara umum.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum-specific suggestions {#quantum-specific-suggestions}"
msgstr "Saran khusus kuantum {#quantum-specific-suggestions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Many of these practices come with special challenges when applied to quantum computing. For example, quantum computing research is often very interdisciplinary, involving researchers from physics, mathematics, and computer science, as well as from application areas like materials science, chemistry, and many more. This could make it difficult to demonstrate requisite expertise on a given research team. Early collaborative work between groups might mitigate this difficulty.\n"
"In the following paragraphs we outline some key considerations in implementing these practices in quantum computing proposals.\n"
msgstr ""
"Banyak praktik ini memiliki tantangan khusus saat diterapkan pada komputasi kuantum. Misalnya, penelitian komputasi kuantum seringkali sangat interdisipliner, melibatkan peneliti dari fisika, matematika, dan ilmu komputer, serta dari bidang aplikasi seperti ilmu material, kimia, dan banyak lagi. Ini bisa menyulitkan untuk menunjukkan keahlian yang diperlukan pada tim penelitian tertentu. Pekerjaan kolaboratif awal antara kelompok-kelompok mungkin dapat mengurangi kesulitan ini.\n"
"Dalam paragraf-paragraf berikut kita menguraikan beberapa pertimbangan utama dalam mengimplementasikan praktik-praktik ini dalam proposal komputasi kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Finding grants**\n"
msgstr "**Mencari hibah**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Start with a thorough overview of grants available to increase chances and "
"optimize fit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mulai dengan tinjauan menyeluruh tentang hibah yang tersedia untuk "
"meningkatkan peluang dan mengoptimalkan kesesuaian.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum computing is a very active area of research and is supported by many"
" government funding institutions including NSF, DoE, DoD, DARPA in the "
"United States, EU Horizon/Quantum Flagship in Europe, and many others.\n"
msgstr ""
"Komputasi kuantum adalah bidang penelitian yang sangat aktif dan didukung "
"oleh banyak lembaga pendanaan pemerintah termasuk NSF, DoE, DoD, DARPA di "
"Amerika Serikat, EU Horizon/Quantum Flagship di Eropa, dan banyak lainnya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are many state-level or regional initiatives focused on the economic "
"effects of quantum computing.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada banyak inisiatif tingkat negara bagian atau regional yang berfokus pada "
"dampak ekonomi komputasi kuantum.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There has been a lot of emphasis on the need for a quantum-smart workforce; "
"many grants will at least have a requirement (if not a focus) on education "
"and workforce development.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada banyak penekanan pada kebutuhan tenaga kerja yang cerdas kuantum; banyak"
" hibah setidaknya akan memiliki persyaratan (jika bukan fokus) pada "
"pendidikan dan pengembangan tenaga kerja.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"See the [section below](#resources)  on grants specific to quantum computing"
" and successful grant writing.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lihat [bagian di bawah](#resources) tentang hibah khusus komputasi kuantum "
"dan penulisan hibah yang sukses.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Match agency initiatives (both strategic goals and timelines).\n"
msgstr "Cocokkan inisiatif lembaga (tujuan strategis maupun timeline).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Many state and national funding opportunities value job upskilling, re-"
"skilling, and training, as well as job creation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Banyak peluang pendanaan negara bagian dan nasional menghargai peningkatan "
"keahlian pekerjaan, pelatihan ulang, dan pelatihan, serta penciptaan "
"lapangan kerja.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider building connections between academia and industry, as well as "
"between educators and institutions with expertise in workforce "
"development.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan membangun koneksi antara akademisi dan industri, serta antara "
"pendidik dan institusi dengan keahlian dalam pengembangan tenaga kerja.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Prior to writing proposal** (these are called out in the proposal "
"itself)\n"
msgstr ""
"**Sebelum menulis proposal** (hal-hal ini disebutkan dalam proposal itu "
"sendiri)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Initial work as proof-of-principle (work that is successful but that cannot "
"be grown without funding).\n"
msgstr ""
"Pekerjaan awal sebagai bukti prinsip (pekerjaan yang berhasil tetapi tidak "
"bisa berkembang tanpa pendanaan).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Very early work could be done using the IBM Quantum Open Plan. For initial "
"exploration of scaling up, consider the IBM Quantum Flex Plan or Pay-as-you-"
"go Plan. See the [IBM Quantum access "
"plans](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/products) for more information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pekerjaan awal sekali bisa dilakukan menggunakan IBM Quantum Open Plan. "
"Untuk eksplorasi awal penskalaan, pertimbangkan IBM Quantum Flex Plan atau "
"Pay-as-you-go Plan. Lihat [rencana akses IBM "
"Quantum](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/products) untuk informasi lebih "
"lanjut.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Demonstrate initiative in building collaborations (intra-university, "
"regionally through Quantum Innovation Centers, nationally).\n"
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan inisiatif dalam membangun kolaborasi (intra-universitas, secara "
"regional melalui Quantum Innovation Center, secara nasional).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Apply for/win seed funding as a multiplier of later grant outcomes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lamar/menangkan pendanaan awal sebagai pengganda hasil hibah selanjutnya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [Quantum Credits program](http://ibm.biz/IBMQuantumCredits) from IBM "
"Quantum may be very useful for showing initial proof-of-principle work, and "
"demonstrating a history of successful grant writing. This program is open to"
" principal investigators at universities and national labs. It is not "
"available to students or members of the broader quantum community.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Program Quantum Credits](http://ibm.biz/IBMQuantumCredits) dari IBM Quantum"
" bisa sangat berguna untuk menunjukkan pekerjaan awal sebagai bukti prinsip,"
" dan menunjukkan riwayat penulisan hibah yang sukses. Program ini terbuka "
"untuk peneliti utama di universitas dan laboratorium nasional. Tidak "
"tersedia untuk mahasiswa atau anggota komunitas kuantum yang lebih luas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**In the proposal**\n"
msgstr "**Dalam proposal**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Call out the preliminary work above.\n"
msgstr "Sebutkan pekerjaan awal di atas.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Propose work that is realistic in terms of timelines, in-house expertise, "
"the state of the science, collaborations, and funds.\n"
msgstr ""
"Usulkan pekerjaan yang realistis dalam hal timeline, keahlian internal, "
"keadaan ilmu pengetahuan, kolaborasi, dan dana.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We estimate that the minimum access for novel quantum computing research "
"requires 400 minutes, which is the minimum purchase limit for the [Flex "
"offering](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/products). Actual needs will vary by "
"project.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kami memperkirakan bahwa akses minimum untuk penelitian komputasi kuantum "
"baru membutuhkan 400 menit, yang merupakan batas pembelian minimum untuk "
"[penawaran Flex](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/products). Kebutuhan aktual "
"akan bervariasi per proyek.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Typically one needs more than 400 minutes, so make sure to allocate a "
"realistic amount for cloud QPU time. \n"
msgstr ""
"Biasanya seseorang membutuhkan lebih dari 400 menit, jadi pastikan untuk "
"mengalokasikan jumlah yang realistis untuk waktu QPU cloud.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Familiarize yourself with the current state of job runtime, qubit counts, "
"and so forth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Biasakan dirimu dengan keadaan terkini runtime job, jumlah qubit, dan "
"sebagainya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Be mindful that the biggest impact applications are likely to leverage both "
"quantum and high-performance computing.​\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa aplikasi dengan dampak terbesar kemungkinan akan "
"memanfaatkan komputasi kuantum dan high-performance computing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* The [advantage tracker](https://quantum-advantage-tracker.github.io/) offers a quick overview of quantum computations that are pushing the limits of what is achievable today.\n"
"Outline institutional resources, facilities, and partnerships that increase feasibility.\n"
"  * Collaborations across disciplines - like computer science, physics, mathematics, chemistry, and others - might help.\n"
"  * Check whether there is a regional Quantum Innovation Center (QIC) in your area. Their technical expertise, access to latest systems, and knowledge of the landscape make them valuable collaborators.\n"
"  * If your institution has centers related to quantum computing, like in cybersecurity, logistics, or biochemistry, see if they have expertise, interest, or other resources available to you.\n"
"* Demonstrate that the problem you are pursuing is important and is not solved, showing mastery of recent progress in the field.\n"
"* Describe the expertise and credentials of the research team.\n"
"  * Showcase interdisciplinary expertise: quantum physicists, device engineers, algorithm theorists, plus HPC expertise for hybrid runs.\n"
"  * Expertise in application areas like chemistry, biochemistry, or materials science may help build a case for broad economic impact.\n"
"  * Highlight IBM Quantum Network membership or cloud credits.\n"
"* List concrete deliverables that are realistic given the resources requested and time constraints.\n"
"  * This can be especially tricky given the pace and novelty of quantum computing.\n"
"  * Make sure to include reliable deliverables include benchmarking, comparisons of methods, scaling studies of new algorithms or new approaches, upskilling, reskilling, and education.\n"
"  * Proof-of-concept calculations followed by scaling studies are more likely to succeed in a funding period than large-scale, very deep circuits and long-term approaches. \n"
"* Acknowledge risks and provide realistic mitigation strategies.\n"
"  * This will be different for every study, but preliminary work using the Flex Plan or through partnership with a QIC will help you identify areas of uncertainty.\n"
"  * Include mitigation strategies. Here \"mitigation\" refers to any project difficulties, but do be sure to outline your intended use of literal error mitigation strategies to show that you will be getting the highest possible performance out of modern quantum computers.\n"
"* Provide a clear, coherent approach with concrete methods, datasets, activities, milestones, and decision points.\n"
"* Address rigor and reproducibility, including data quality, controls, analysis, and sharing.\n"
"  * Include open-source commitments (for example, Qiskit extensions) to meet NSF data-sharing mandates and enable broader impacts\n"
"* Draw connections between academia and industry, and broader impacts generally\n"
msgstr ""
"* [Pelacak keunggulan](https://quantum-advantage-tracker.github.io/) menawarkan gambaran singkat tentang komputasi kuantum yang mendorong batas-batas apa yang dapat dicapai saat ini.\n"
"Uraikan sumber daya, fasilitas, dan kemitraan institusional yang meningkatkan kelayakan.\n"
"  * Kolaborasi lintas disiplin - seperti ilmu komputer, fisika, matematika, kimia, dan lainnya - mungkin membantu.\n"
"  * Periksa apakah ada Quantum Innovation Center (QIC) regional di areamu. Keahlian teknis mereka, akses ke sistem terbaru, dan pengetahuan tentang lanskap menjadikan mereka kolaborator yang berharga.\n"
"  * Jika institusimu memiliki pusat yang berkaitan dengan komputasi kuantum, seperti di keamanan siber, logistik, atau biokimia, lihat apakah mereka memiliki keahlian, minat, atau sumber daya lain yang tersedia untukmu.\n"
"* Tunjukkan bahwa masalah yang kamu kejar penting dan belum terpecahkan, menunjukkan penguasaan kemajuan terkini di bidang ini.\n"
"* Jelaskan keahlian dan kredensial tim penelitian.\n"
"  * Tunjukkan keahlian interdisipliner: fisikawan kuantum, insinyur perangkat, ahli teori algoritma, ditambah keahlian HPC untuk eksekusi hybrid.\n"
"  * Keahlian dalam bidang aplikasi seperti kimia, biokimia, atau ilmu material mungkin membantu membangun argumen untuk dampak ekonomi yang luas.\n"
"  * Soroti keanggotaan IBM Quantum Network atau kredit cloud.\n"
"* Daftarkan deliverable konkret yang realistis mengingat sumber daya yang diminta dan batasan waktu.\n"
"  * Ini bisa sangat rumit mengingat kecepatan dan kebaruan komputasi kuantum.\n"
"  * Pastikan untuk menyertakan deliverable yang dapat diandalkan termasuk benchmarking, perbandingan metode, studi penskalaan algoritma baru atau pendekatan baru, peningkatan keahlian, pelatihan ulang, dan pendidikan.\n"
"  * Kalkulasi bukti konsep diikuti oleh studi penskalaan lebih mungkin berhasil dalam periode pendanaan daripada circuit yang sangat dalam berskala besar dan pendekatan jangka panjang.\n"
"* Akui risiko dan berikan strategi mitigasi yang realistis.\n"
"  * Ini akan berbeda untuk setiap studi, tetapi pekerjaan awal menggunakan Flex Plan atau melalui kemitraan dengan QIC akan membantumu mengidentifikasi area ketidakpastian.\n"
"  * Sertakan strategi mitigasi. Di sini \"mitigasi\" mengacu pada kesulitan proyek apapun, tetapi pastikan untuk menguraikan penggunaan strategi mitigasi error yang dimaksud untuk menunjukkan bahwa kamu akan mendapatkan performa tertinggi yang mungkin dari komputer kuantum modern.\n"
"* Berikan pendekatan yang jelas dan koheren dengan metode, dataset, aktivitas, milestone, dan titik keputusan yang konkret.\n"
"* Tangani ketelitian dan reproduktibilitas, termasuk kualitas data, kontrol, analisis, dan berbagi.\n"
"  * Sertakan komitmen open-source (misalnya, ekstensi Qiskit) untuk memenuhi mandat berbagi data NSF dan memungkinkan dampak yang lebih luas\n"
"* Bangun koneksi antara akademisi dan industri, serta dampak yang lebih luas secara umum\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Potentially important points unique to the quantum computing industry**\n"
msgstr "**Poin-poin penting yang unik untuk industri komputasi kuantum**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"State specifically why you want to use the architecture/systems you propose."
" For example, you might structure your proposal around fixed-frequency "
"transmon qubits like those in IBM&reg; quantum computers for the following "
"reasons:\n"
msgstr ""
"Nyatakan secara khusus mengapa kamu ingin menggunakan arsitektur/sistem yang"
" kamu usulkan. Misalnya, kamu mungkin menyusun proposal-mu di sekitar qubit "
"transmon frekuensi tetap seperti yang ada di komputer kuantum IBM&reg; "
"karena alasan berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"They have very fast gate times and can perform many operations within the "
"coherence time\n"
msgstr ""
"Mereka memiliki waktu gate yang sangat cepat dan dapat melakukan banyak "
"operasi dalam waktu koherensi\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "They have high gate fidelity\n"
msgstr "Mereka memiliki fidelitas gate yang tinggi\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"They have a predictable scalability according to the IBM Quantum Roadmap\n"
msgstr ""
"Mereka memiliki skalabilitas yang dapat diprediksi sesuai dengan IBM Quantum"
" Roadmap\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You might focus on the scale and accessibility of quantum computers for the "
"following reasons:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu mungkin berfokus pada skala dan aksesibilitas komputer kuantum karena "
"alasan berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IBM quantum computers are the largest QPUs available, unlocking utility-"
"scale work for true innovation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Komputer kuantum IBM adalah QPU terbesar yang tersedia, membuka pekerjaan "
"skala utilitas untuk inovasi sejati.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Anything smaller than IBM quantum computers can be done on a simulator.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apapun yang lebih kecil dari komputer kuantum IBM dapat dilakukan pada "
"simulator.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You might call out the architecture of a specific processor like Nighthawk, "
"and its suitability for quantum error correction.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu mungkin menyebut arsitektur prosesor tertentu seperti Nighthawk, dan "
"kesesuaiannya untuk koreksi error kuantum.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Technical feasibility of projects {#technical-feasibility-of-projects}"
msgstr "Kelayakan teknis proyek {#technical-feasibility-of-projects}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The limits of what is possible in quantum computing are changing every day. But it is important to keep the current constraints in mind in outlining your project. For detailed information on each quantum computer, and even on each qubit, check out the [compute resources page](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) on [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/). \n"
"The following high-level technical information might be useful. These are not hard limits that apply to all circumstances, but general guidelines to be adapted to your specific case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Batas-batas apa yang mungkin dalam komputasi kuantum berubah setiap hari. Tetapi penting untuk mengingat batasan saat ini dalam menguraikan proyekmu. Untuk informasi terperinci tentang setiap komputer kuantum, dan bahkan setiap qubit, lihat [halaman sumber daya komputasi](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) di [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/).\n"
"Informasi teknis tingkat tinggi berikut mungkin berguna. Ini bukan batas keras yang berlaku untuk semua keadaan, tetapi panduan umum yang harus diadaptasi untuk kasus spesifikmu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Qubit count** - IBM Nighthawk processors have 120 qubits. Some systems "
"have slightly more. These systems offer utility-scale research for novel "
"discoveries that are not classically accessible.  \n"
msgstr ""
"**Jumlah qubit** - Prosesor IBM Nighthawk memiliki 120 qubit. Beberapa "
"sistem memiliki sedikit lebih banyak. Sistem-sistem ini menawarkan "
"penelitian skala utilitas untuk penemuan baru yang tidak dapat diakses "
"secara klasik.  \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Circuit depth** - The maximum circuit depth depends on many factors. Be "
"sure you are considering the transpiled depth of two-qubit gates as the "
"primary measure of depth. Transpiled, two-qubit depths around 30 are often "
"manageable with modern error suppression and mitigation techniques. A few "
"niche applications might encounter difficulties at lower depths, and some "
"circuits can certainly go beyond that. This is a good depth at which to "
"explore.  \n"
msgstr ""
"**Kedalaman circuit** - Kedalaman circuit maksimum bergantung pada banyak "
"faktor. Pastikan kamu mempertimbangkan kedalaman transpile dari gate dua-"
"qubit sebagai ukuran kedalaman utama. Kedalaman dua-qubit yang ditranspile "
"sekitar 30 seringkali dapat dikelola dengan teknik suppression dan mitigasi "
"error modern. Beberapa aplikasi niche mungkin mengalami kesulitan pada "
"kedalaman yang lebih rendah, dan beberapa circuit tentu bisa melampaui itu. "
"Ini adalah kedalaman yang baik untuk dijelajahi.  \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**QPU time** - This is entirely dependent on your application. We estimate "
"that a minimum of 400 minutes is required for novel quantum computing "
"research. You might also check the QPU time required for individual runs of "
"the projects listed on the advantage tracker. Most fall between 30-120 "
"minutes. When we allow for experimentation, benchmarking of your problem, "
"and multiple attempts, this time range is consistent with the aforementioned"
" minimum.  \n"
msgstr ""
"**Waktu QPU** - Ini sepenuhnya bergantung pada aplikasimu. Kami "
"memperkirakan bahwa minimum 400 menit diperlukan untuk penelitian komputasi "
"kuantum baru. Kamu juga mungkin memeriksa waktu QPU yang diperlukan untuk "
"eksekusi individual proyek yang terdaftar di pelacak keunggulan. Sebagian "
"besar berkisar antara 30-120 menit. Ketika kita memperhitungkan "
"eksperimentasi, benchmarking masalahmu, dan beberapa percobaan, rentang "
"waktu ini konsisten dengan minimum yang disebutkan di atas.  \n"

